# trigger|match|package. Matches a detected device to an extras.list row. Used by Hardware Detect.
# match is a lowercase vendor id (PCI or USB), a CPU vendor_id, or * for any. package must equal the extras.list package field exactly.
# hybrid means a laptop with more than one GPU vendor.
cpu|genuineintel|intel-microcode
cpu|authenticamd|amd64-microcode
gpu|8086|firmware-intel-graphics intel-media-va-driver
gpu|1002|firmware-amd-graphics mesa-va-drivers
gpu|10de|firmware-nvidia-graphics nvidia-detect nvidia-driver nvidia-kernel-dkms
wifi|8086|firmware-iwlwifi
wifi|10ec|firmware-realtek
wifi|0bda|firmware-realtek
wifi|168c|firmware-atheros
wifi|0cf3|firmware-atheros
wifi|14e4|firmware-brcm80211
wifi|14c3|firmware-mediatek
wifi|0e8d|firmware-mediatek
bluetooth|*|bluez
audio|8086|firmware-sof-signed
hybrid|*|switcheroo-control
sensors|*|lm-sensors
